WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.760
Planning conditions hold up the start on site.

2
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.590
Send us the decision notice. That is the whole brief.

3
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:21.013
Every condition is put into plain English: what the council needs, when it is due, which specialist usually prepares it and which documents to gather.

4
00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:27.572
In this sample, 7 conditions must be dealt with before work can start.

5
00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:37.027
You get the register with the conditions that block a start picked out, plus a drafted covering letter for each council submission.

6
00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:45.749
Every entry in the register sets out the condition as written in the decision notice, so each point can be checked against the original.

7
00:00:47.049 --> 00:00:54.849
We do not give planning advice. We do not submit anything to the council. You or your planner remain responsible.

8
00:00:56.149 --> 00:01:01.428
Condition Desk. £400 per permission. Usually within a day.

